WEBVTT

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:04.360
 From our free daily newsletter, the latest from podnews.net with

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:05.400
 Magellan AI.

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:10.350
 Podcast Movement has revealed featured speakers for the event in

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:12.700
 New York City in September.

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:17.850
 Among the speakers are Greg Glenday, the CEO of Acast, Beehiiv's

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:20.120
 Ainsley Rossitto and me.

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:23.820
 Sounds Profitable's Tom Webster will also be unveiling new

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:26.400
 research. Tickets are available now.

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:31.600
 Alex Cooper's Unwell Network has received a strategic investment

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:34.020
 from WTSL, an investment firm.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:36.790
 The investment figure isn't known, but according to The

00:00:36.790 --> 00:00:41.240
 Hollywood Reporter, values Unwell at $500 million.

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:45.510
 Just to put that into context, the entirety of iHeartMedia is

00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:48.680
 currently valued at $450 million.

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:52.880
 Another set of podcasts have signed with Disney+.

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:56.860
 This time, it's from the UK, as The Overlap signed a landmark

00:00:56.860 --> 00:01:00.180
 sponsorship and distribution deal with Disney+,

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:03.270
 for its Stick to Football show, and a new show focusing on

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:04.600
 Manchester United.

00:01:05.140 --> 00:01:08.930
 The shows will remain available on YouTube, though Disney+, will

00:01:08.930 --> 00:01:11.990
 also get access to additional special episodes of Stick to

00:01:11.990 --> 00:01:12.760
 Football.

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:16.840
 The Sounds Profitable Business Summit unveiled its first set of

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:19.320
 speakers, including Ira Glass.

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:22.820
 Representatives from YouTube and Amazon are also to speak.

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:26.420
 The event is exclusive to Sounds Profitable Partners and takes

00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:29.360
 place September the 14th to the 15th.

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:31.740
 Pod News will be reporting from the event.

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:36.660
 A new ad tech tool called Vaudeo has launched, which promises to

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:39.080
 make video ads from audio spots.

00:01:39.580 --> 00:01:43.280
 It should unlock $12 million of new revenue for creators, the

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:44.740
 company suggests.

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:46.140
 What's a podcast?

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:48.540
 We have a short definition.

00:01:48.940 --> 00:01:51.460
 If it works with your eyes closed, it's a podcast.

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:57.280
 But Signal Hill Insights asked more than 4,800 Americans how Ved

00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:01.070
 describe what a podcast is to someone who has never heard of

00:02:01.070 --> 00:02:01.920
 podcasts.

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:05.560
 Willing to those today, not sure that something people waste

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:08.740
 time watching or listening to is going to catch on.

00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:12.980
 And Oxford Road's Media Roundtable podcast this week reacts to

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:17.180
 our story last week about Spotify's new ad-skipping tool.

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:21.500
 Dan Granger and Jars Martin are joined by Glenn Rubenstein of Adopter

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:25.880
 Media, who suggests that the button is, quote, fundamentally

00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:26.580
 wrong.

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:31.900
 In People News, congratulations to Audacia Audio's Kim Treasure,

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:35.010
 who's the winner of the Entrepreneur Award at Media Week

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:36.920
 Australia's Next of the Best.

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:40.790
 Also, congratulations to Candace Wilson from Your Podcast

00:02:40.790 --> 00:02:44.550
 Producer, who appeared on a recent episode of BBC Radio 4's

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:48.200
 Woman's Hour, giving advice on how to start a podcast.

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:53.340
 And also to John Harvey, podcaster of Trash Talk and Independent

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:58.380
 Space Warrior, who, wearing a bin on his head, is standing in a

00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:01.860
 British election today against a toad.

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:06.510
 And in podcast news, recorded less than a mile from Stamford

00:03:06.510 --> 00:03:10.130
 Bridge, Out of the Blue is a new weekly Chelsea FC podcast,

00:03:10.130 --> 00:03:11.860
 which kicks off today.

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:15.610
 It's produced by Footwork Media and features a rotating cast of

00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:19.610
 diehard blues who'll break down the latest match action, tackle

00:03:19.610 --> 00:03:23.060
 the endless noise and off-pitch developments around the club,

00:03:23.060 --> 00:03:25.260
 and look ahead to upcoming fixtures.

00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:30.610
 And from the surround podcast network, Ideas of Order returns

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:32.900
 for a new season this week.

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:37.460
 The first guest is Antoni Porowski, who's a Queer Eye star, chef,

00:03:37.460 --> 00:03:42.420
 author and television personality, who joins host Jeremiah Brent

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:47.110
 to discuss memory, identity and the rituals that make a house

00:03:47.110 --> 00:03:48.600
 feel like a home.

